CAVEAT: WP2 was trained on TRANSPARENT objects; ZeroWaste rigid_plastic
  includes OPAQUE rigid plastics, so IoU-vs-rigid_plastic understates
  perception if it correctly ignores opaque items. Hit-precision is the
  class-mismatch-independent read: high hit-precision = coherent masks on
  real objects (graceful degradation); low = hallucinating on background.

CONTRAST FOR SYNTHESIS:
  policy on these SAME frames: 0% on-target, ~100% gibberish output.
  if hit-precision is well above 0, the front-end degrades gracefully
  where the policy collapses -> 'perception transfers, policy does not'.

